WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.462
This is your first guided practice Choose either
Task A or Task

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:08.388
B and write the query in the editor For Task A
return

00:00:08.412 --> 00:00:11.888
MRN patient name and age for all patients and sort
from oldest

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:17.662
to youngest Start by identifying the three columns
for SELECT The source

00:00:17.675 --> 00:00:22.062
table is patients Because the task says all patients
you do not

00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:25.938
need a WHERE clause The phrase oldest to youngest
tells you to

00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:30.588
order age descending For Task B return active
patients who are age

00:00:30.612 --> 00:00:34.438
fifty or older and sort age descending This time you
need two

00:00:34.462 --> 00:00:37.788
WHERE conditions active status must be true and age
must be at

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.762
least fifty Connect the two conditions with AND Try
to write the

00:00:42.788 --> 00:00:47.500
query before opening or relying on the check
information Use the earlier

00:00:47.525 --> 00:00:52.225
slides as patterns SQL work is often about adapting
a pattern to

00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:56.088
a new question After you run the query do not stop
at

00:00:56.112 --> 00:01:01.575
the message that it executed Inspect the rows For
Task A the

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.162
reset dataset should return six rows and the oldest
patient should appear

00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:09.762
first For Task B verify both the active status idea
and the

00:01:09.775 --> 00:01:13.988
age threshold If your result is wrong change one
part at a

00:01:14.012 --> 00:01:18.550
time Check the selected columns then the WHERE
condition then the ORDER

00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:19.238
BY clause
